# Architecture and ownership

- Follow `docs/architecture-principles.md` (Rules 1–12). Changing them requires an ADR and Joel approval.
- Respect module ownership in `docs/modules/`. Do not take ownership of another module’s records.
- Distinguish Current vs Intended vs Future in `docs/architecture.md`. Do not claim unimplemented features exist.
- Accepted proposals / historical commercial records: version or supersede—do not silently overwrite.
- Cross-module access must use documented service/repository boundaries.
- Do not change existing functionality incidentally while working on an unrelated feature.
